     "result_text_tail": "eckpoint.\n\nThe deck also has an options comparison, a risks slide with test and trigger points, a 2027 plan with the four decisions requested, and appendices with every calculation.\n\nI made these choices where I would have asked you:\n- **Format:** a 16:9 PowerPoint file, with sources and assumptions in footers and appendices.\n- **Pro adoption:** 25% in the base case. That sits between the paywall rate (14%) and the 33% who moved to the higher tier launched in 2023.\n- **Allowance and overage:** 600 AI requests per seat per month, pooled per account, and $20 per extra 1,000 requests. These are my proposals; the pack doesn't contain these figures.\n- **Effect of the mobile rewrite:** I assume it halves mobile-driven churn, and I show a case where it ends it.\n- **Platform cost:** I counted the $0.6M a year as cost of revenue, which is the cautious choice for the margin test.\n\nThere is one inconsistency in the pack. The top 10% of beta accounts average 14,500 requests a month, which works out to 40% of all requests, not the 58% the pack states. The deck uses the higher-cost figure and asks Product to reconcile the two.\n\nI couldn't open the file in PowerPoint or Keynote here because the sandbox blocks them. Instead I checked every slide with my own previews, built from the same layouts, and fixed all the text overflows they showed. The text, charts and tables are all editable. The \u2713/\u2717 symbols in tables rely on PowerPoint's font fallback, so check they display when you first open it."
